WEBVTT

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:04.890
when working with documents there may be

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:07.290
occasions where you need to protect the

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:10.290
document which will restrict access or

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:11.969
editing rights to the document as you

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:13.320
can see I have a demonstration document

00:00:11.969 --> 00:00:15.030
on the screen in front of me and I'm

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.880
going to demonstrate how you can apply

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:20.310
to password to access to fail and also a

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:23.400
password to restrict any editing of the

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:25.019
document the next thing I need to do is

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.380
I need to navigate up to the top toolbar

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:30.869
and select the tools option and then

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.880
from the drop down the protect document

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:36.510
option this brings up the password

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.370
protect dialog box so in the very first

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.809
one which is set as password to open

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:43.950
this document I will just type in

00:00:39.809 --> 00:00:49.500
password press ENTER and it will ask me

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:53.010
to enter that again and select ok if I

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.719
click here now that is set the password

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:57.449
but that won't be active till I've

00:00:54.719 --> 00:01:00.359
actually see after document so if I just

00:00:57.449 --> 00:01:02.070
go to file and I'll close the document

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:06.930
and they'll ask me if I want to see that

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:11.270
select yes so now the forms that when I

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:11.270
open that it will ask for a password

00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:18.900
select your key and that will then open

00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:20.850
the document another option is is to

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:24.030
restrict the editing of the document as

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:26.220
you can see at the moment I can probably

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:29.670
cursor in the document and make changes

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:31.500
I'll just don't do those changes so what

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.659
I need to do is I need to restrict the

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.939
editing so if I click on the tools' mint

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:38.869
button again and go down to protect

00:01:35.939 --> 00:01:42.360
document and I'll just take off the

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:46.049
password I will then enter a password to

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:47.460
modify the document so anybody who

00:01:46.049 --> 00:01:54.810
wishes to modify it must have the

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:59.939
password click it and ask the password

00:01:54.810 --> 00:02:01.590
again select ok and again this won't be

00:01:59.939 --> 00:02:06.000
active until I save the document so I'm

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:09.330
going to go to fail and Clause and then

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:12.510
make sure I select see if so now when I

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:13.240
click on it it will ask me for a

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:14.740
password

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:16.270
so if I want to modify that I must put

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:18.040
the password in I can't open the

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:19.710
document but I would have to click read

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.930
only if I didn't have the password and

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:25.720
then I would not be able to make any

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:27.130
changes no matter what I pressed they

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.630
could make a duplicate copy of the

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:31.240
document may changes but the original

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:33.280
copy would not be changed there's no way

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:35.940
anybody could change that without having

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:35.940
the actual password